  "term": "secure base",
  "definition": "In this attachment-related usage, secure base refers to using an attachment figure, such as a caregiver or owner, as a base for exploring and interacting with the environment without anxiety. The packet describes it as one of the behavioral components of attachment and notes that, in children and dogs, this effect can influence exploration and performance in cognitive testing.",
